# cornerpin

- Label: Corner Pin
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 38 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/cornerpin.html
- Summary (EN): The Corner Pin node sets the corner positions of a layer relative to a reference layer, so the texture is stretched to fit between those corners. The output is sized to the reference. Listed as available since 21.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Corner Pin étire une texture entre quatre coins définis par rapport à une couche de référence, avec une transformation en perspective si la caméra l'est.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: reference layer the texture is rasterised into", "texture: layer whose corners are pinned"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by source", "Units: Image (-1 to 1 over display window), Texture (0 to 1 over data window), Pixels (absolute), World (projected through the layer's implicit camera)", "Bottom Left, Bottom Right, Top Left, Top Right: corner positions, interpreted according to Units"]

- Caveats: ["If the reference layer has a perspective camera, use world-position corners to get a perspective transform; otherwise the result is an affine stretch"]

